From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: announce LDPC reception

The AC PHY decodes LDPC with bit 6 of PHY register 0x01b0 set, the bit
wl 7.14's wlc_phy_update_rxldpc_acphy() switches, and b43's PHY init
leaves it set (0xa6cb on both radios, as under wl). Announce it on HT
and VHT, as the stock driver does. mac80211 then also sends LDPC to a
station that receives it, which b43 already lays out.

With a OnePlus Nord 2 (two streams, RX LDPC) two rooms away on 5 GHz
ch36/80 (-70 to -79 dBm): uplink 97-121 Mbit/s against 69-114 without,
and the downlink 156-176 with LDPC against 126-156 with it switched off
in a test build, alternating in the same position.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -7231,9 +7231,13 @@ static const struct ieee80211_iface_comb
  *    and VHT MCS 0-9 go out on up to the txchain's, in the layout of the
  *    stock drivers' descriptors (b43_txhdr_ac_ht(), b43_txhdr_ac_vht());
  *  - the long MPDUs and A-MSDUs, beyond the receive buffer;
- *  - LDPC reception, beamformee and the link adaptation the stock driver
- *    announces on VHT: nothing configures or decodes them; SU beamformer
- *    is announced and done (b43_txbf_link()). A VHT frame is
+ *  - beamformee and the link adaptation the stock driver announces on VHT:
+ *    nothing configures or decodes them; SU beamformer is announced and
+ *    done (b43_txbf_link()).
+ *
+ * LDPC reception is announced on HT and VHT, as the stock driver does: the
+ * PHY decodes it with bit 6 of 0x01b0 set (wlc_phy_update_rxldpc_acphy()
+ * of 7.14), which the PHY init leaves set (0xa6cb, as under wl). A VHT frame is
  *    sent with LDPC when mac80211 asks, for a station that receives it, as
  *    every VHT frame of the stock driver's is.
  *
@@ -7261,6 +7265,7 @@ static void b43_ac_set_ht_vht_cap(struct
 	memset(ht, 0, sizeof(*ht));
 	ht->ht_supported = true;
 	ht->cap = IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SUP_WIDTH_20_40 |
+		  IEEE80211_HT_CAP_LDPC_CODING |
 		  IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_20 |
 		  IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_40 |
 		  (WLAN_HT_CAP_SM_PS_DISABLED << IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SM_PS_SHIFT);
@@ -7282,6 +7287,7 @@ static void b43_ac_set_ht_vht_cap(struct
 	memset(vht, 0, sizeof(*vht));
 	vht->vht_supported = true;
 	vht->cap = IEEE80211_VHT_CAP_MAX_MPDU_LENGTH_3895 |
+		   IEEE80211_VHT_CAP_RXLDPC |
 		   IEEE80211_VHT_CAP_SHORT_GI_80 |
 		   IEEE80211_VHT_CAP_MAX_A_MPDU_LENGTH_EXPONENT_MASK;
 	vht->vht_mcs.rx_mcs_map = cpu_to_le16(map);
